# Snyk auth (PAT preferred)

`.github/workflows/security-scans.yml` uses **SNYK_TOKEN** (Snyk Personal Access Token) when set. Legacy fallback: **SNYK_OAUTH_TOKEN** from `snyk auth` (~1h expiry).

## Preferred setup (PAT)

1. Create PAT in Snyk → Account settings → Personal access tokens.
2. GitHub repo secret: `gh secret set SNYK_TOKEN` (or `scripts/set-snyk-pat-secret.ps1`).
3. Cursor Cloud Agent secrets: same `SNYK_TOKEN` for "Weekly Snyk vulnerability scan & fix" automation.
4. Optional: delete `SNYK_OAUTH_TOKEN` from GitHub after PAT works.

## Legacy OAuth (fallback only)

1. `snyk auth` then `scripts/refresh-snyk-oauth-secret.ps1` — expires ~1h; re-run after each auth.
2. Offer refresh script only when PAT is unavailable and CI/auth fails.

## On any Snyk request

1. Prefer PAT flow; do not suggest hourly OAuth refresh if PAT is an option.
2. MCP `user-Snyk` may error without valid local auth; CLI + CI workflow is primary.
3. Keep Snyk in security-scans.yml alongside Trivy, Semgrep, Gitleaks, etc.
4. CI severity threshold is **medium** (parity with Cursor automation).
